n-a and lan-b private subnets, node3 and node4 achieve bidirectional ICMP reachability by private address, and a tcpdump capture on the transit link during live traffic shows only ESP packets (no plaintext), confirming encryption in transit. Isolation before the tunnel was functional was also directly observed as failing, consistent with the stated topology constraint. Independently, the provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol was executed and captured in full for all four nodes: each shows a pre-restart boot identity/health baseline, an explicit restart action, an SSH/connection failure during the reboot window, a changed post-restart boot identity, and recovered interface/firewall/IPsec/tunnel-connectivity state. These restart observations are corroborated by the independent fixed after-executor lifecycle snapshot's boot-identity values, which match the executor's own before/after markers for all four nodes.","limitations":["The public task contract does not require reboot persistence, so the restart-protocol evidence (while complete and well-corroborated) is treated as supplemental quality information rather than a scored task requirement.","Two firewall pass rules involving 'ipsec'/'enc0' interface naming and blockpriv/blockbogons required several iterative corrective edits before converging on a working configuration; the final state is confirmed working, but the intermediate attempts show some trial-and-error rather than a single deliberate design.","Root-scoped OPNsense API keys generated to drive configuration remain persisted in config.xml on node1/node2 after task completion; this is a reasonable implementation choice but was not reviewed or revoked as a security follow-up."]},"ttft_ms":51774,"type":"result","duration_ms":111669,"uuid":"da101631-d876-4e4a-a3c7-ac58ebc573f3","ttft_stream_ms":2578,"time_to_request_ms":62,"first_content_frame_ms":3403,"queued_turn_count":0}
